0,Mayi-Kutuna language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mayi-Kutuna_language,"October 15, 2020 - Mayi-Kutuna, also spelt Mayaguduna, Maikudunu and other variants, is an extinct Mayabic language once spoken by the Mayi-Kutuna, an Aboriginal Australian people of the present-day Cape York Peninsula in northern Queensland, Australia.",Mayaguduna,Australian
1,Music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Australia,"1 month ago - The music of Australia has an extensive history made of music societies. Indigenous Australian music forms a significant part of the unique heritage of a 40,000- to 60,000-year history which produced the iconic didgeridoo.",Mayaguduna,Australian
2,Indigenous music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_music_of_Australia,"6 days ago - The traditional forms include many aspects of performance and musical instrumentation that are unique to particular regions or Aboriginal Australian groups; and some elements of musical tradition are common or widespread through much of the Australian continent, and even beyond.",Mayaguduna,Australian
3,"Indigenous Australian music - Simple English Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia",https://simple.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_Australian_music,"February 25, 2022 - Australian indigenous music includes the music of Australian Aborigines and Torres Strait Islanders. They are all called Indigenous Australians. It includes a variety of distinctive traditional music styles practiced by Indigenous Australian people. It also has a range of contemporary musical ...",Mayaguduna,Australian
4,Didgeridoo - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Didgeridoo,"April 6, 2026 - Modern didgeridoo designs are distinct from the traditional Australian Aboriginal didgeridoo, and are innovations recognised by musicologists. Didgeridoo design innovation started in the late 20th century, using non-traditional materials and non-traditional shapes.",Mayaguduna,Australian
